Z||000000||PatrickB||10-26-2000||07:46 PM||||My brother has an MX6 or something like that and when he came home from work today he was telling me that when he was at the gas station he had the car idling for a few minutes and he noticed that a lot of coolant had spilled on the floor.  But the car wasnt overheating.  I checked it when he got home and I couldnt find any leak.  The coolant resevoir was empty so I filled it back up.  I had the car running, the temp guage went to normal, and no coolant was leaking.  If the water pump goes bad does it leak out of the weep hole all the time?  I doubt that much coolant would come out anyway.<BR>Another thing was that the car was hissing while running.  I dont know if it does this all the time but I dont think so.<BR>Sound like anything to anybody?<P>Pat||||reg||5
Z||000001||ur2biteme||10-26-2000||09:20 PM||||check radiator cap seals.  when they stop holding proper pressure, they allow boiling to occur<P>------------------<BR>UR2BITEME<BR>'87 econo coupe<BR>170k and a bad fender :(||||reg||1
